<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15736" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-năto</span></b> , āvi,
			1, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to swim out</i> or <i>away</i>,
				<i>to escape by swimming</i> (very rare).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 6
				praef.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. A. P. 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 4,
				21, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. M. p. 121, 3
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to extricate one's
				self</i>, <i>to get off</i>: reliqui habere se
			angustius videntur; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">enatant tamen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 5, 30, 87</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Petr. 57, 10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
